1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,850
Unpaid toll text?

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,170
Don't tap it.

3
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:04,670
Check it like this.

4
00:00:05,029 --> 00:00:06,159
find your state's toll

5
00:00:06,109 --> 00:00:07,439
service yourself.

6
00:00:07,649 --> 00:00:08,699
Use the website on

7
00:00:08,649 --> 00:00:10,339
your own toll statement,

8
00:00:10,329 --> 00:00:11,419
the website printed on

9
00:00:11,369 --> 00:00:13,199
your toll transponder account,

10
00:00:13,149 --> 00:00:14,319
or search for your

11
00:00:14,269 --> 00:00:15,959
state's official toll agency

12
00:00:15,909 --> 00:00:16,979
and type the address

13
00:00:16,929 --> 00:00:18,119
in yourself.

14
00:00:18,369 --> 00:00:18,999
Log in to your

15
00:00:18,949 --> 00:00:20,639
account there, or call

16
00:00:20,589 --> 00:00:21,859
the customer service number

17
00:00:21,809 --> 00:00:22,639
you found on your

18
00:00:22,589 --> 00:00:23,259
own.

19
00:00:23,449 --> 00:00:24,799
That's exactly what the

20
00:00:24,749 --> 00:00:26,499
FBI and the FTC

21
00:00:26,449 --> 00:00:27,799
both tell people to

22
00:00:27,749 --> 00:00:28,499
do:

23
00:00:28,529 --> 00:00:29,639
check your account through

24
00:00:29,589 --> 00:00:31,279
the legitimate website,

25
00:00:31,229 --> 00:00:32,399
or call the real

26
00:00:32,349 --> 00:00:33,979
customer service number.

27
00:00:34,169 --> 00:00:35,179
If you really do

28
00:00:35,129 --> 00:00:36,259
owe a toll, it

29
00:00:36,209 --> 00:00:37,279
will be there.

30
00:00:37,349 --> 00:00:38,339
If it isn't,

31
00:00:38,289 --> 00:00:39,419
you've just stopped a

32
00:00:39,369 --> 00:00:40,139
scam.

